# This repository is the six-app ecosystem only. The working directory it lives
# in also holds unrelated projects, so the root is a whitelist rather than a
# blocklist: anything not named below is never a candidate for a commit.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/Makefile
!/scripts/
!/cadence/
!/timbre/
!/segue/
!/gamut/
!/ostinato/
!/concerto/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
*.egg-info/

# Caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Corpora. The Million Playlist Dataset is licensed for research use and must
# not be redistributed; the audio-feature dump is a 12 GB reproducible download.
# Both are re-fetchable -- see cadence/scripts/download_data.py.
# Anchored to the repo root on purpose. A bare `data/` matches a directory of
# that name at ANY depth, which also swallowed cadence/src/cadence/data/ -- real
# source code, silently absent from the first four commits. `cadence build`
# could not have run from a fresh clone.
/cadence/data/

# Build outputs. Model weights, cached sequences and embedding matrices are all
# reproducible from a fixed seed, and several are hundreds of megabytes. The
# rendered reports and the small JSON each is generated from are kept: they are
# the evidence behind every number quoted in the docs.
*/artifacts/*
!*/artifacts/results.html
!*/artifacts/*_report.json
!*/artifacts/demo.json
!*/artifacts/*_meta.json
# Concerto writes four: three are small, and sensitivity.json is ~430 KB because
# it holds every one of the 180 parameter cells. It is kept anyway -- the claims
# in the README are "held in N of 180", and without the cells that is an
# assertion rather than evidence. It regenerates in about eight minutes.
!*/artifacts/simulation.json
!*/artifacts/sensitivity.json
!*/artifacts/ledger.json
!*/artifacts/calibration.json
!*/artifacts/frontier.json
